  "about": {
    "parts": "The default part binding, for a model that gives none of its own: the bones that may weight each part of a trunk, a head, a neck built apart from the trunk, the limbs, hands and feet, and a tail. The trunk allows the upper arms and the upper legs: the loop of a welded armhole or leg hole belongs to the trunk, and a loop that takes no weight from the limb's first bone, while the limb's ring beside it does, can break when the limb moves. A hand allows the mitten fingers; a rig without them keeps the hand bone alone.",
    "roll": "Every bone's Z axis points forward (-Y) at rest, so limbs bend about a common axis; tail bones point Z up.",
    "options": "The sets of optional bones a rig may have: tail, the number of bones of the tail chain from the hips (0: no tail); hands, 'plain' for the hand bone alone or 'mitten' for the mitten fingers (Index, Middle, Thumb) hanging off each hand unconnected. Every bone not marked optional is required; an optional bone belongs to the rig exactly when an option requires it.",
    "poses": "The review poses: bone-local Euler XYZ rotations in degrees from the rest pose. The right side mirrors the sign of Z, the finger curl included. A bone the rig lacks (an optional bone) is left out of a pose."
  }
